# Dealership booking constraints

- Source of truth: `CONTEXT.md`, `docs/prd/`, `docs/trd/`, `docs/decision/`, `docs/testing/`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/adr/`.
- Do not write application code (`pom.xml`, `src/`, Docker images) unless the user **explicitly** asked to implement. Discussion → docs only.
- Use glossary terms. Appointment not booking. Reminder vs Notification are different.
- No Lombok. Record DTOs. Explicit JPA entities. UUID primary keys.
- Comments in Java: only non-obvious why. See `docs/trd/comments.md`.
- Reuse, no redundancy, lean diffs: `docs/trd/code-style.md`. One page/access/time/Reminder-SQL/sender/`ApiErrorCode`/`Inputs`.
- API docs: springdoc-openapi (Swagger UI), see `docs/trd/openapi.md`. Authorize is OAuth2 password (username = email), not paste-only Bearer. Not springfox.
- JPA for CRUD. Native SQL / JdbcTemplate for SKIP LOCKED, due-time insert, send-window expire, no-show UPDATE. Do not hydrate full graphs to do clock math.
- Redis = Bucket4j token bucket HTTP limits only, **per endpoint**, **15 / 60s** (window never longer than 60s). Postgres = ledger (Reminders, one Confirmed per Vehicle when `APP_ONE_CONFIRMED_PER_VEHICLE=true`).
- Staff create Appointments at home Dealership only.
- List GETs paginated **and searchable** (`page`, `size`, `q`). Default `size` **100**, max **1000**. Nested refs batched (`findAllById` / `findByCustomerIdIn`), not per-row `findById`. Appointment reads: own or home Dealership, else 404. Staff `GET /customers` (and `/customers/{id}/vehicles`) to obtain ids for booking — home Dealership membership required, else 404. Staff `POST /customers` and `POST /customers/{id}/vehicles` for walk-ins. Staff `GET /appointments/{id}/reminders` for Reminder + Notification (`offsetMinutes`, `dueAt` UTC, always-present `notification`, `NOT_SCHEDULED` until a row exists) and `lastError` (home Dealership); replay is `POST /notifications/{id}/replay` at that home Dealership only. Replay reopens the Reminder to `PROCESSING` with a live lease so `MailWorker` can send.
- `APP_JWT_SECRET` ≥ 32 bytes or the process does not start. Non-`dev`/`test` also refuses the committed default secret. `make run` defaults to `dev`; production must omit that profile.
- Reminder offsets, no-show grace, JWT, workers, pagination, rate limits, and `APP_ONE_CONFIRMED_PER_VEHICLE` from env/config. Status/role columns are PostgreSQL ENUM + Java enum, not `varchar`. Reminder offsets are `APP_REMINDER_OFFSETS` (`24h,2h` default; add `7d`, `6h`) stored as `offset_minutes`, not an enum.
- Reminder offsets from config. No confirmation mail. Workers 2–4, lease heartbeat. **Claim Batch** auto from CPU count (`APP_WORKERS_CLAIM_BATCH=0`, floor 18 for 500k/day = 10× assignment 50k, max 50). Hikari/Tomcat also auto unless pinned.
- Shop-floor In Progress is later. Completed is v1. Staff at home Dealership complete, cancel, and reschedule Confirmed visits. Customers cancel and reschedule their own. Customer complete → 403; other shop / other customer → 404. Do not invent In Progress.
- Never log raw contact, User name, or full **Vehicle Number**. Default Notification Mode is stub. `notify: false` appends `logs/notifications.log`; `notify: true` uses stub or SMTP.
- Duplicate Reminder prevention must be a unique constraint plus a test, not an application `if`.
- Store Appointment `scheduled_at` as UTC **and** `display_offset` from `scheduledAt`. No Customer timezone in the payload. Mail/Customer GET use Booking Offset. Staff GET uses Dealership Timezone. JVM UTC so EC2 host zone never leaks. Never print UTC as the only time in mail. Clock math is set-based SQL.
- Idempotency-Key TTL 24h, unique per User. Expired `idempotency_keys` purged at UTC midnight. Notification `idempotency_key` is not TTL-purged.
